                <pb facs="0327" n="257" sameAs="frus:frus1934v04/pg257"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/3800: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Geneva</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gilbert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-06-07T10:00:00+01:00">June 7, 1934—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 7—7:17 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>140. Arms embargo. British Delegation informs me that London has taken action
                    indicated in Consulate’s 135, June 5, 2 p.m., paragraph 1.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gilbert</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
